92186045417] [17592186341700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341700 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341700 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341700 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341700 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186340043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341700 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b6c41871-59a4-56ef-80fe-7d004904e3a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342241 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342241 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74599" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342241 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342241 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $c=⟨1,-6,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,-10,-15⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342241 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6c3f74b-5a27-519e-8d22-1736702759dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342241 #edb/ref 1074 "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t=1 \\\\ 4s-6t=-10 \\\\ 3s-7t=-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t=1 \\\\ -2t=-6 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-6\\,⟹\\,t=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+3 & =1 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot 3=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186363424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186363424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363419 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "669d7279-38d4-5150-94a0-6a97a679c0f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363420 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363420 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363420 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d4e7ea98-c99e-5e1a-b0a7-704c7552fe2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363421 #edb/ref 1080 "n\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363421 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186363421 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "516f0376-d461-50f1-9446-88d42e4dd246" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
